      <div class="art-media">SKILLS MISMATCH</div>
      <div class="art-body">
        <p class="art-meta">Editorial &middot; Job-oriented mindset</p>
        <h3>The educated-unemployment paradox</h3>
        <p>Roughly 700,000 graduates enter Bangladesh&rsquo;s job market each year, but the
        formal economy generates only about 300,000 viable roles. What that gap does to how
        students think about the point of a degree.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
<div class="article-card">
      <div class="art-media">THE MEMORIZATION TRAP</div>
      <div class="art-body">
        <p class="art-meta">Editorial &middot; Innovation &amp; critical thinking</p>
        <h3>Escaping the memorisation trap</h3>
        <p>SSC and HSC exams still reward textbook repetition over comprehension. What
        that costs in independent thought &mdash; and what a competency-based curriculum
        would need to change on the ground.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
<div class="article-card">
      <div class="art-media">EDUCATION &amp; MONEY</div>
      <div class="art-body">
        <p class="art-meta">Editorial &middot; Perceptions of education</p>
        <h3>Education = money? Rethinking what learning is for</h3>
        <p>For many families, a degree is a financial investment first &mdash; a ticket
        exchanged for a stable job. This pilot asks what gets lost when employment becomes
        education&rsquo;s only measure of success.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
